declare extern type AnimationTrack with
    --- Whether the track is advancing. It becomes false when a track that is not `Looped` reaches the
    --- end of its clip. Such a track keeps showing its last frame until it is stopped or played again.
    read Playing: boolean
    --- Whether the track starts again when it reaches the end of its clip. A looped track never fires
    --- `Ended`.
    Looped: boolean
    --- How fast the clip plays. 2 is twice as fast and half as long. 0 holds the current pose.
    Speed: number
    --- How much this track contributes when several tracks animate the same skeleton. Setting it takes
    --- effect immediately; to fade a track in or out, pass a fade time to `Play` or `Stop`. Tracks are
    --- blended as a weighted average for each joint. A joint that no playing clip animates keeps its
    --- rest pose.
    Weight: number
    --- The duration of the clip, in seconds, or 0 if the clip was not found.
    read Length: number
    --- The current position in the clip, in seconds.
    read TimePosition: number
    --- A signal that fires on the tick a track that is not `Looped` reaches the end of its clip. `Stop`
    --- does not fire it, so code that starts the next animation from this signal is not triggered by an
    --- interrupted one.
    read Ended: Signal<>
