    --- How much of the pose comes from the simulation, from 0 (none) to 1 (all). The blend is between
    --- two poses: each driven joint is drawn between where the animation puts it and where its limb
    --- part is. It does not weaken the simulation; the limb parts fall the same way at any value. Ramp
    --- it from 0 to 1 over a few tenths of a second to make a character go down without a visible snap,
    --- and back to 0 to make it get up.
    Blend: number
    --- Creates the limbs of the ragdoll from a profile and returns how many it made. For each joint the
    --- profile names, it creates a `Part`, a `Bone` on the part that names the joint, and a constraint
    --- to the limb above. The limbs are created at the rig's current pose. Everything it creates is an
    --- ordinary instance that you can select, move, adjust and delete. Run it once in the editor and
    --- save the scene, and the ragdoll is part of the scene with no script needed. A profile is an
    --- ordered list of limbs. `require("@engine/ragdoll").Humanoid` is a built-in profile that fits
    --- common humanoid rigs. Each entry is a table: - `Joint`: the joint's name, or a list of names
    --- tried in order. - `Parent`: the 1-based index of the limb this one hangs from; omit it for the
    --- root. It must refer to an earlier entry. - `Radius`, `LeafLength`: the capsule's radius, and the
    --- length of a limb that has nothing below it. Otherwise a limb's length is the distance to the
    --- joint below it. - `Kind`: `"BallSocket"`, `"Hinge"` or `"Fixed"`. - `Swing`, `Twist`: for a ball
    --- socket, the cone half-angle and the twist range, in degrees. - `LimitLow`, `LimitHigh`: for a
    --- hinge, the range in degrees. A limb whose joint the rig does not have is skipped, and its
    --- children hang from the nearest limb that was built. Raises an error if the ragdoll is not under
    --- a skinned `MeshPart`, if it already has limbs, if the profile is malformed, or if the rig has
    --- none of the profile's joints.
