declare extern type Sound extends Instance with
    --- The audio file, as an `asset://` path. WAV, MP3, FLAC and Ogg Vorbis are supported. A file of up
    --- to ten seconds is decoded once and kept in memory. A longer file is streamed, so a long music
    --- track uses about as much memory as the size of its file. The length of the sound is the length
    --- of the file, and `Ended` fires when `TimePosition` reaches it. A path to a file that does not
    --- exist plays a one-second placeholder tone instead of silence, so that a missing file is noticed.
    --- `DebugService:GetStat("AudioClipsMissing")` returns how many sounds are missing their file.
    Content: Content
    --- Whether the sound is advancing. Setting it resumes or pauses the sound at `TimePosition`; it
    --- never rewinds. Use `Play` to start from the beginning and `Stop` to stop and rewind.
    Playing: boolean
    --- Whether the sound starts again when it reaches the end. A looped sound never fires `Ended`.
    Looped: boolean
    --- A multiplier on the loudness of the sound, combined with its group's volume and with the falloff
    --- over distance. The default is 0.5, which leaves headroom when several sounds play at once.
    Volume: number
    --- How fast the sound plays, which also changes its pitch. 2 is an octave higher and half as long.
    --- It must be greater than 0; use `Playing` to pause.
    PlaybackSpeed: number
    --- The current position in the sound, in seconds, from 0 to `TimeLength`. Set it to seek. A value
    --- below 0 raises an error. A value beyond the end is clamped to the end, or wrapped if the sound
    --- is `Looped`.
    TimePosition: number
    --- The length of `Content`, in seconds. It is the length of the file, or one second for the
    --- placeholder tone of a missing file. It is 0 until the length has been read, which happens on the
    --- first tick after `Content` is set. A sound recorded in several languages is as long as its
    --- longest recording. The value is the same on every machine whatever language each one plays, so
    --- `Ended` fires on the same tick everywhere. A shorter recording is followed by silence. A sound
    --- with a `Caption` and no file in any language lasts as long as its caption is shown.
    read TimeLength: number
    --- The distance from the listener within which a positional sound plays at its full `Volume`, in
    --- meters. Beyond it the sound gets quieter. A sound that is not positional ignores it.
    RollOffMinDistance: number
    --- The distance from the listener at which a positional sound becomes silent, in meters. Between
    --- `RollOffMinDistance` and this distance, the volume falls off linearly.
    RollOffMaxDistance: number
    --- The `AudioGroup` whose volume this sound's volume is multiplied by, or nil for none.
    Group: AudioGroup?
    --- The kind of sound: `Effects`, `Music` or `Voice`. It selects which of the player's volume
    --- settings applies (`AudioService.EffectsVolume`, `MusicVolume` or `VoiceVolume`). Music is
    --- automatically lowered while a voice plays. The category is replicated with the sound, unlike
    --- `Group`, which is local to each machine.
    Category: EnumSoundCategory
    --- How loud the recording is at the current moment on this machine, from 0 to 1. It is the level of
    --- the recording over about the last twentieth of a second at `TimePosition`; a full-scale tone
    --- reads 1. Use it to open a character's mouth while a line plays. It is the level of the recording
    --- itself. No volume setting and no distance affects it. It is measured on the language this
    --- machine plays, so it differs between machines; do not use it in game rules. It is 0 while the
    --- sound is not playing, during the silence after a shorter language, and for a sound with no file.
    read Loudness: number
    --- Fires on the tick a sound that is not `Looped` reaches its end. The sound stops and
    --- `TimePosition` returns to 0. It fires on the same tick in a replay, in a headless run and on
    --- every machine.
    read Ended: Signal<()>
    --- Fires when the sound's `Content` is ready to play. It currently fires immediately.
    read Loaded: Signal<()>
    --- Returns the level that `Loudness` measures, split into three frequency bands, each from 0 to 1.
    --- The bands are low (80 to 500 Hz), middle (500 to 2,500 Hz) and high (2,500 to 10,000 Hz). A
    --- full-scale tone inside one band reads 1 in that band and 0 in the others. Use it to tell an open
    --- mouth from a wide or a round one, or to drive a visualizer. The bands are computed only when
    --- requested, and once per tick however many times they are requested. Like `Loudness`, the result
    --- differs between machines.
    function GetBands(self): (number, number, number)
    --- Plays the sound from the start, or from `TimePosition` if a script set it since the sound last
    --- started. Calling it on a sound that is already playing restarts it. To continue after `Pause`,
    --- use `Resume`. The language of the sound is chosen when it starts. `Content` is looked for under
    --- `l10n/<VoiceLocale>/`, then under the language without its region, then at the path as written.
    --- A sound that is playing finishes in the language it started in.
    function Play(self): ()
    --- Continues the sound from `TimePosition`, where `Pause` left it. It is the same as setting
    --- `Playing` to true.
    function Resume(self): ()
    --- Stops the sound at its current position. `Resume` continues from there, and `Play` starts again
    --- from the beginning. It is the same as setting `Playing` to false.
    function Pause(self): ()
    --- Stops the sound and rewinds it to the start. `Ended` does not fire.
    function Stop(self): ()
end

