declare extern type Swarm extends Instance with
    --- The position every agent walks toward, unless `SetTargets` has given other targets.
    Target: vector
    --- Whether the swarm updates. When it is off, its agents stay where they are.
    Enabled: boolean
    --- The side of the cells of the grid in which agents find their neighbors, in meters. Set it to
    --- about the diameter of the widest agent.
    CellSize: number
    --- The largest number of neighbors an agent considers each tick. It limits the cost of a tightly
    --- packed crowd.
    MaxNeighbors: number
    --- Deprecated: use `MaxNeighbors`. The old name still works.
    MaxNeighbours: number
    --- The acceleration at which an agent falls, in meters per second squared.
    Gravity: number
    --- The speed at which an agent climbs over the agent in its way, in meters per second.
    ClimbSpeed: number
    --- How high the crowd can pile on itself, in meters above the ground under an agent. 0 means no
    --- limit. Above this height, an agent does not climb the agent in its way, and an agent standing on
    --- one that tall is pushed aside and comes down. A limit of two or three agents' heights looks like
    --- a wave breaking over an obstacle. With no limit, a crowd around a stationary obstacle builds a
    --- tower over it.
    PileHeight: number
    --- The distance from `Target`, beyond the agent's own radius, at which an agent stops walking
    --- toward it.
    StopDistance: number
    --- The distance from `Target`, in meters, beyond which an agent is updated every second tick.
    NearDistance: number
    --- The distance from `Target`, in meters, beyond which an agent is updated every fourth tick.
    FarDistance: number
    --- Whether the swarm's agents are replicated to the other machines in a multiplayer match. When it
    --- is on, each client has this swarm with the same agent numbers, read-only. On a client,
    --- `GetAgents`, `GetPositions`, `GetAgentPosition`, `GetAgentTag` and `QueryRadius` return results,
    --- `AgentAdded`, `AgentRemoved` and `AgentTagChanged` fire, and `SetAgentBody` gives an agent a
    --- local body to move. An agent's state is sent to a client when the client's copy would otherwise
    --- be drawn wrong, and the client moves the agent itself in between. A client's agent is therefore
    --- close to the authority's position but not exactly at it; decide hits on the authority. A client
    --- has only the agents within `ReplicationRadius` of its player's focus. When it is off, the swarm
    --- exists only on the machine that runs it.
    Replicates: boolean
