    --- machine until `AgentRemoved` fires for it, and can be reused after that.
    read AgentAdded: Signal<number, number, vector>
    --- Fires when this machine loses an agent. Passes the agent's last tag and position, and the
    --- reason: the authority removed it, or, on a client, it left the client's replication radius. Play
    --- a death effect for the first reason and nothing for the second.
    read AgentRemoved: Signal<number, number, vector, EnumSwarmAgentRemoval>
    --- Fires when the tag of an agent that this machine has changes.
    read AgentTagChanged: Signal<number, number>
    --- Adds an agent at the position of `body` and returns its number. The options are `Radius`
    --- (default 0.5), `Height` (1) and `Speed` (4, in meters per second). `Floats` keeps the agent
    --- `FloatHeight` (1) above the ground, where the crowd does not push it. `Climbs` (true) lets it
    --- climb over the agent in its way. The number identifies the agent while it exists and is reused
    --- for a later agent after this one is removed. For an agent with no body, use `AddAgentAt`.
    function AddAgent(self, body: BasePart, settings: { Radius: number?, Height: number?, Speed: number?, Floats: boolean?, FloatHeight: number?, Climbs: boolean? }?): number
    --- Adds an agent that has no body, with its feet at `position`, and returns its number. The swarm
    --- simulates it and nothing is drawn. Use it on a server that simulates a horde for clients that
    --- draw it themselves: read the agents with `GetPositions` and send what the clients need. The
    --- options are those of `AddAgent`.
    function AddAgentAt(self, position: vector, settings: { Radius: number?, Height: number?, Speed: number?, Floats: boolean?, FloatHeight: number?, Climbs: boolean? }?): number
    --- Sets several positions for the agents to walk toward, such as every player in a match. Each
    --- agent walks toward the nearest one, and its update rate (`NearDistance`, `FarDistance`) depends
    --- on its distance to that one. Call it again whenever the positions change. An empty table goes
    --- back to using `Target` alone.
    function SetTargets(self, targets: { vector }): ()
    --- Removes an agent from the swarm. Its body stays where it is and is no longer moved.
    function RemoveAgent(self, agent: number): ()
    --- Sets how fast an agent walks, in meters per second. At 0 the agent stays in place, and other
    --- agents still push it.
    function SetAgentSpeed(self, agent: number, speed: number): ()
    --- Moves an agent to a position. It falls to the ground from there.
    function SetAgentPosition(self, agent: number, position: vector): ()
    --- Knocks an agent back with a velocity along the ground, in meters per second, that fades quickly.
    function Push(self, agent: number, velocity: vector): ()
    --- Returns the position of an agent, or nil if there is no such agent.
    function GetAgentPosition(self, agent: number): vector?
    --- Returns the number of every live agent, in slot order. If `into` is given, that table is
    --- cleared, filled and returned, so a script that calls this every tick allocates nothing.
    function GetAgents(self, into: { number }?): { number }
    --- Returns the position of every live agent, in the order `GetAgents` returns them. If `into` is
    --- given, that table is cleared, filled and returned.
    function GetPositions(self, into: { vector }?): { vector }
    --- Returns every live agent whose feet are within `radius` of `center`, in slot order. Use it to
